  "slug": "astrometric-precision-incoherent-4af7",
  "summary": "Six preprints test scalar-field dark energy and inflationary features against CMB, DESI, Pantheon+ and JWST, and add clustering and pulsar-timing probes.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is confronting extensions of ΛCDM with combined datasets. Two papers address the Hubble tension with scalar-field dark energy: a double-power potential unifying early and late dark energy against CMB, DESI BAO and Pantheon+, and axion early dark energy combined with JWST high-redshift galaxy abundances, which reports H0≈72.76 km/s/Mpc. A third searches for oscillatory primordial power spectrum features from axion monodromy inflation using Planck PR4, DESI DR2, Pantheon+ and ACT/SPT. The remaining items extend the toolkit: a hybrid Lagrangian bias expansion for post-reconstruction galaxy clustering, interpretable neural marked statistics targeting non-Gaussian information, and NANOGrav 15-yr binary-pulsar orbital perturbations constraining ultralight dark matter couplings. What is new is the joint use of DESI-era and JWST data with these models and methods.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
